export SHARED_AGENT_REPORTING:
    obligation:
        Agent reporting is optional enrichment under the drop-in
        contract, not a prerequisite for installing the dashboard:
        the core dashboard works read-only from the host's existing
        identity and lifecycle. Where a consuming application adopts
        agent reporting, agents must automatically provide task status,
        timing, progress, estimated completion, usage, limits, and
        limit projections through one shared format across agents and
        harnesses. Agents must make available information explicit;
        missing harness telemetry does not remove the reporting
        obligation once reporting is adopted. Information an agent
        cannot obtain or reasonably estimate must be explicitly unknown.
    formatBoundary:
        The consuming application defines one concrete serialization
        and transport for this shared contract. All reporting agents
        use it; harness-specific inputs are mapped into the same concepts.
    reportContent:
        - Run, task, agent, and harness identity for correlating reports.
        - A distinct attempt identity for each task retry.
        - An increasing report sequence number within each task attempt.
        - Task status and the time the reported information was updated.
        - Running time, or timing information from which it can be derived.
        - Task progress and estimated time to completion.
        - Usage, applicable limits, and projected time to reaching each limit.
        - Whether each metric is observed, estimated, or unknown.
        - Associated software build jobs and their execution locations when applicable.
    metricSemantics:
        Include units for numeric metrics and the scope of usage limits
        when known. Include reset information when available. Label
        estimates and preserve unknown values without inventing data.
    automaticUpdates:
        Report when task status changes and periodically while tasks
        are running, without waiting for a user to request an update.
        A harness hook or background reporter maintains heartbeats while
        an agent is busy or blocked. Heartbeats indicate reporter health;
        each task metric retains its own last-checked time. Sending a
        heartbeat alone does not refresh task status or metrics.
    progressReporting:
        Agents report their own approximate percent complete of the whole
        task, with a short note on what they are doing, about every ten
        minutes and at each milestone. The consuming application gives every
        agent an exact reporting command or call in its task instructions,
        filled in with that agent's run, task and attempt identity, so an
        agent never has to work out its identity. Reported progress is the
        agent's estimate, labeled as such, carries its own last-checked
        time, and goes stale like any other metric. A task that has never
        reported shows progress as unknown. Agent-reported progress never
        replaces a derived completion estimate; both are shown.
    harnessOnlyTasks:
        Work that a harness shows but that sends no reports of its own, for
        example a session started before reporting existed, is shown as a
        harness-only row with its unknown metrics, never hidden.
    configurableDefaults:
        reportingIntervalSeconds: 10
        staleAfterSeconds: 30
        missedHeartbeatsBeforeStale: 3
    defaultRationale:
        These are initial operational defaults chosen under the user's
        request to use reasonable timing. The consuming application
        may configure them for its environment.

export REPORTING_OPEN_QUESTIONS:
    - What serialization and transport will implement the shared reporting contract?
